{"timestamp": "2026-10-07T02:02:34.866204+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3B_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3B", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "OFFLINE", "red_team": "OFFLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "DEBATE_PROPOSAL", "agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist", "proposal_text": "Excellent questions. The rigor you're describing is precisely what underpins our analysis, allowing us to provide a reliable diligence signal for your team.\n\n1.  **GitHub Metadata**: We apply a logarithmic decay function to commit recency and a Gini coefficient to contributor diversity. The reason we measure this is to filter out vanity commits and manufactured activity, which gives your team a trusted signal to differentiate genuine development momentum.\n\n2.  **Team Execution Power**: It\u2019s a weighted composite of commit velocity, PR merge latency, and contributor diversity. The reason we calculate this is to quantify a team\u2019s operational discipline, which gives your team a fast, objective signal that saves hours of manual review.\n\n3.  **Data Pipeline**: Our on-chain data has <1 min lag from our dedicated nodes; off-chain is polled at 15-min intervals. This ensures your decisions are based on near-real-time data.\n\n4.  **Predictive Pillars**: Back-testing shows Team Execution and Tokenomic Resilience have the highest correlation with post-Series A follow-through.\n\nThis deep, structured data is how we deliver fast, auditable analysis to augment your team\u2019s capacity on demand. When is a good time to walk through a 